2026.10.11 - TheFantasticsIssue

→ “An Extraordinary Year, Answered by Them: Fantastic Man Who ___”

In an era where time’s anchor points can be freely set, the “year” is no longer defined by the passing of natural calendar years, but rather marked by each of us and every change unfolding around us.

On the first anniversary of @FantasticMan官方, we have remained committed to creativity and a local perspective, delivering in-depth insights and content that often ventures beyond conventional boundaries, capturing the faces worthy of being remembered by our times.

Every October, “Yi Zhou Fantastic Man” pays tribute to the year’s most remarkable individuals with its anniversary issue. In this #非凡一年#:

Antoine Arnault, Head of Image and Environment at LVMH Group, opened up 71 locations across 13 countries for 45 of the group’s brands;

Designer Dries Van Noten chose not to pause, instead establishing a cultural foundation;

Cinematographer and director Christopher Doyle meticulously chronicled half a century of light, shadow, and spiritual exploration through pen and paper;

Artist Liu Jianhua embarked on a new chapter in his creative journey;

Stage visual artist @任冬生REN painted light and color onto stages, bringing forth more than a thousand performances of “Only Blue Green”;

The architectural firm Snøhetta built a Chinese fan along Shanghai’s Huangpu River;

Director @文牧野, after delivering three feature films, continues to weave stories yet untold;

Art historian and curator Wu Hung traverses time and space through books and exhibitions;

Freestyle skier @王心迪Freestyle, after a 20-year hiatus, once again secured China’s first-ever Olympic gold medal in men’s aerials;

Actor and singer @王一博·YIBO placed himself within different speeds—climbing rock walls and racing down tracks.

“The Fantastics Issue” of “Yi Zhou Fantastic Man,” titled “An Extraordinary Year,” will walk alongside and engage in dialogue with those who have answered the call of this remarkable year.

*Individuals are listed in alphabetical order

